SOAPBOX: I love WPX and was looking forward to the contest. Found a quiet
SOAPBOX: spot on the bands a few times to call CQ and had some good runs
SOAPBOX: when not distracted, the S&P rate wasn't too bad, either. I had
SOAPBOX: half-heartedly thought about making 1M points my goal for the
SOAPBOX: contest, which in hindsight wasn't a very lofty goal somewhere
SOAPBOX: around the 500-QSO mark I realized that 1000 QSO's was well
SOAPBOX: within reach and made that the new goal. Achieved, with some
SOAPBOX: wiggle room for when the LCR hits.
SOAPBOX: My first foray as an
SOAPBOX: "official" PVRC member - GO PVRC!
SOAPBOX: 40m netted the most
SOAPBOX: points-per-QSO, but at the expense of rate. 15m is my favorite,
SOAPBOX: where I spent the most time, and netted the most QSO's. 20m was
SOAPBOX: acting a bit strange this weekend it opened late, but also gave
SOAPBOX: a late-night opening Saturday night into Sunday morning - VK's,
SOAPBOX: SA, EU all simultaneously - although even with a little bit of
SOAPBOX: power and a baby yagi, working stations that were S4+ was still
SOAPBOX: at times a challenge.
SOAPBOX: Positives: met my goal(s), didn't break
SOAPBOX: anything, propagation was at least "good", only heard one
SOAPBOX: instance of on-air fighting over a frequency (and only stuck
SOAPBOX: around to listen because I was hoping to work a new mult haha),
SOAPBOX: and had plenty of fun.
SOAPBOX: Gripes: could've worked a few more
SOAPBOX: stations if the over-driven stations nearby calmed it down. If
SOAPBOX: I'm ever 4kHz wide and splattering I hope somebody has the
SOAPBOX: courtesy to tell me I much prefer hearing unsolicited
SOAPBOX: compliments on having clear audio. 40m had plenty more stations
SOAPBOX: but all below 7.125 - wasn't that long ago that listening above
SOAPBOX: 7.200 was common for them but now it's just a case of "look but
SOAPBOX: don't touch" for the mults hiding down there. Only mistaken as
SOAPBOX: KP4ZZ a handful of times may be my last entry as K4PZZ depending
SOAPBOX: on how the FCC lottery goes.
SOAPBOX: FT-2000, SB-200, TA-33 @ 40ft, doublet @ 40-ish ft, N1MM+.
